ce/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,4,1),$ $Q(3,4,2)$ and $R(3,3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/state.json" "file_sha256" "d1c3c5666e14ee210e237c0c1918a47251637f00dd4def28595311827c8b7293" "basis" 2540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $P,$ $Q$ and $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,4,1⟩,\\,q=⟨3,4,2⟩,\\,r=⟨3,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨3,4,2⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨3,3,1⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})={60}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/state.json" "file_sha256" "d1c3c5666e14ee210e237c0c1918a47251637f00dd4def28595311827c8b7293" "basis" 2540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e5fe340aa1f5295cfe7753920c41e9c55e95894989c68b4d30c32ec2b3bd557d" "basis" 2540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/state.json" "file_sha256" "d1c3c5666e14ee210e237c0c1918a47251637f00dd4def28595311827c8b7293" "basis" 2540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{30}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/state.json" "file_sha256" "d1c3c5666e14ee210e237c0c1918a47251637f00dd4def28595311827c8b7293" "basis" 2540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{45}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_