7c8b7293" "basis" 2540 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,1,2)$, $Q(1,3,2)$, and $R(4,5,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,1,2⟩,\\,q=⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,r=⟨4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,3,2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨4,5,-2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,4,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5})≈{63}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69439c99388ed4f03cb7c64633545f69bd84ad1aacf06d4f3cc7b3d16b3e60a7" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{27}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" "selection