 "value" [:answer.type/math "{63}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-1,0,3)$, $Y(-2,2,3)$, and $Z(-2,-1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,y=⟨-2,2,3⟩,\\,z=⟨-2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69439c99388ed4f03cb7c64633545f69bd84ad1aacf06d4f3cc7b3d16b3e60a7" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{120}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{30}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{45}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{60}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{90}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-19039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $m\\cdot n=10$, find the angle between $m=⟨t,-t,3⟩$ and $n=⟨3,2,4⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-19039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $m\\cdot n=10$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\\cdot n & =10 \\\\ t\\cdot 3+(-t)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4 & =10 \\\\ 3t-2t+12 & =10 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =⟨(-2),-(-2),3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $m$ and $n$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{m\\cdot n}{|\\,m\\,||\\,n\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{m}_{x}{n}_{x}+{m}_{y}{n}_{y}+{m}_{z}{n}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{m}_{x}^{2}+{m}_{y}^{2}+{m}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{n}_{x}^{2}+{n}_{y}^{2}+{n}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{17}\\cdot \\sqrt{29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{493}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{493}})≈{63.23}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-19039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "233850fe09862b35c978ccd0ab32f2824a6b64ebf4a8d50d31489bf66768bcfc"} {"question" "q-19039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-19039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{41.76}^{∘}"] ["math" "{54.98}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60.87}^{∘}"] ["math" "{63.23}^{∘}"] ["math" "{88.21}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-19039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{63.23}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,1,2)$, $Q(1,3,2)$, and $R(4,5,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,1,2⟩,\\,q=⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,r=⟨4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,3,2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨4,5,-2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,4,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5})≈{63}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "233850fe09862b35c978ccd0ab32f2824a6b64ebf4a8d50d31489bf66768bcfc"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{27}^{∘}"] ["math" "{57}^{∘}"] ["math" "{63}^{∘}"] ["math" "{88}^{∘}"] ["math" "{90}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{63}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-1,0,3)$, $Y(-2,2,3)$, and $Z(-2,-1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,y=⟨-2,2,3⟩,\\,z=⟨-2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "233850fe09862b35c978ccd0ab32f2824a6b64ebf4a8d50d31489bf66768bcfc"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{120}^{∘}"] ["math" "{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60}^{∘}"] ["math" "{90}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{45}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,4,1),$ $Q(3,4,2)$ and $R(3,3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $P,$ $Q$ and $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,4,1⟩,\\,q=⟨3,4,2⟩,\\,r=⟨3,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨3,4,2⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨3,3,1⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})={60}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "233850fe09862b35c978ccd0ab32f2824a6b64ebf4a8d50d31489bf66768bcfc"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60}^{∘}"] ["math" "{75}^{∘}"] ["math" "{90}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-77159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{60}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-101514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $a\\cdot b=-10$, find the angle between $a=⟨-4t,3t⟩$ and $b=⟨2,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-101514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $a\\cdot b=-10$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-10 \\\\ (-4t)\\cdot 2+3t\\cdot 1 & =-10 \\\\ -8t+3t & =-10 \\\\ -5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨-4(2),\\,3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10}{\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{10\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}})≈{116.6}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-101514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "233850fe09862b35c978ccd0ab32f2824a6b64ebf4a8d50d31489bf66768bcfc"} {"question" "q-101514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071968/state.json" "file_sha256" "84efee784599eb06fb9d5d25384da4a6e41e55c4194011f7298f2608fbe52869"} {"question" "q-101514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{111.1}^{∘}"] ["math" "{113.8}^{∘}"] ["math" "{116.6}^{∘}"] ["math" "{120.9}^{∘}"] ["